ly state that MultiMeshInstance2D (or rather MultiMesh with 2D Transforms) make use of physics interpolation (https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.html#other). After some fiddling I discovered that this was not the case.\r\n\r\nSo here is a hopefully decent implementation I basically replicated MultimeshInstance3D behaviour to MultiMeshInstance2D and added mesh_storage for 2D transforms.\r\n\r\nEdit:\r\nSmall Testproject: [MultiMesh2D_Interp_Test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20795528/MultiMesh2D_Interp_Test.zip)\r\n\r\n(Use space bar to toggle physics interpolation for the meshinstance on/off)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url"